# Step 9 & 10: App Component (Root Layout)

> **Note on Modern Angular (v17+ / v20):**
> If your project uses standalone components (default in modern Angular), you must import `HeaderComponent` and `HomeComponent` into the `imports` array of `app.component.ts` so the custom tags can be recognized.

# `src/app/app.component.ts`

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { HeaderComponent } from './components/header/header.component';
import { HomeComponent } from './pages/home/home.component';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  standalone: true,
  imports: [HeaderComponent, HomeComponent],
  templateUrl: './app.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./app.component.css']
})
export class AppComponent {
  title = 'student-course-portal';
}

```

*(If your project is using traditional `NgModule` architecture, ensure `HeaderComponent` and `HomeComponent` are listed in `app.module.ts` under `declarations`.)*

# `src/app/app.component.html`

Replace all boilerplate content in `src/app/app.component.html` with:

```html
<app-header></app-header>
<main>
  <app-home></app-home>
</main>

```

